prefixOpT -- SEQ 597 R2 (Tony, 2026-11-10): PIN, DO NOT CURE. Every Operators entry in a prefix position, where it has no
target: as an assignment's right side (qr = <op> qb; print qr:;) and as a print item (print <op> qb:;), on the old road
(the statements at top level) and the new road (the same statements through FILe), then print "Q" and a sentinel.

Each value reads: [stdout, lines joined by |] r<REFUSED lines> p<of those, the "in a prefix position with no target"
wording> x<exit status> s<sentinel reached>.

INTENDED for an entry that is not a unary (class n): refused by name, one wording, and the next statement runs --
[0 |Q |] r1 p1 x0 s1 for the assignment (qr keeps its 0) and [Q |] r1 p1 x0 s1 for the print item. The old road is there
already on nearly every entry. The new road is not: it uses the operand, or refuses with another wording, or prints
the token as text, and on 16 entries the run DIES at exit 139 with no sentinel, 27 runs in all (qr = / qb is one). The cure is its own
later stroke. A unary entry (class u: declared unary, or in the UnaryOPS bin) is pinned at today's value and has no
intended value here. A second mention of += in setup (its member block) is one entry and one row.

Not run alone: pop.sh builds four inputs per row. Fields are separated by TABS (operators use | and ^).

